+# 0034. Agent Conformance And WinDAGs Directive Gate
+
+## Status
+
+Proposed — 2026-05-16
+
+## Context
+
+Port Daddy now launches and observes agents across several runtime families:
+Claude Code / Claude CLI / Claude SDK, Codex CLI, Gemini, Cloudflare Workers
+AI, Moonshot/Kimi through the Cloudflare model ladder, Ollama, Aider, and
+custom wrappers. The operator also expects those agents to use Port Daddy and
+WinDAGs rather than treating them as optional advice.
+
+The failure mode is not only file collision. The harder failure is path
+dependence: two individually reasonable directives can combine into a broken
+product, a stomped worktree, a stale PR, a missing citation, a sycophantic plan,
+or a runtime that claims coordination while `agentId` is null.
+
+Port Daddy already has the pieces:
+
+- Navigator/Cartographer owns roadmap and recovery-map truth
+  (`docs/adr/0023-cartographer-roadmap-actor.md`).
+- Spider surfaces new opportunities and unSpider finds contradictions
+  (`docs/adr/0031-spider-surface-finder.md`,
+  `docs/adr/0032-unspider-contradiction-finder.md`).
+- Coordination Guard enforces claim-aware staging.
+- WinDAGs provides a 5-stage planning pipeline and a skill catalog through
+  `next-move`, `skillful-node-prompt`, and MCP tools such as
+  `windags_skill_search`, `windags_skill_graft`, `windags_skill_reference`, and
+  `windags_history`.
+
+Those pieces need to become a launch contract, not a set of suggestions.
+
+## Decision
+
+Port Daddy will add a fail-closed **Agent Conformance Gate** in front of every
+mutation-capable agent launch and every Port Daddy-brokered LLM call.
+
+The gate creates a durable `conformanceRecord` before launch. A record is valid
+only when it proves:
+
+1. **Identity:** non-null `agentId`, `identityProject`, purpose, telos, backend,
+   model tier, worktree, branch, and parent operator directive.
+2. **Isolation:** an explicit harbor/container/worktree/sandbox boundary with
+   write scope and network/MCP capability policy.
+3. **Port Daddy session:** a live or freshly created session, a scope note, and
+   intended file/region claims before file mutation is allowed.
+4. **WinDAGs planning:** at least one skill-search result, grafted primary
+   skills for non-trivial work, a directive-regression DAG, and node input /
+   output contracts.
+5. **Cartographer ordering:** current directive is checked against active
+   roadmap slices, recovery work, claims, PRs, and in-flight missions.
+6. **Adversarial review:** unSpider or a successor risk actor estimates bugs,
+   security issues, UX failures, prompt failure, and feature interactions before
+   work starts.
+7. **Prompt wrapper:** the final provider prompt includes Port Daddy operating
+   rules, non-sycophancy instructions, scope boundaries, citation requirements,
+   escalation rules, and repair-on-substrate-failure rules.
+8. **Reviewer pass:** a cheaper reviewer model checks the proposed launch prompt
+   or output for sycophancy, unsupported non-trivial assertions, missing
+   citations, and conformance drift.
+9. **Telemetry:** launchability, exact model/rate/cost policy, and backend
+   readiness are proven before operator-facing launch.
+
+If any required field is missing, the gate blocks. In particular,
+`agentId: null` has no write authority.
+
+## Spirit Of The Request
+
+The operator's directive is not "make agents say they coordinate." It is:
+
+- Treat every objective as part of one evolving product, not as an isolated
+  ticket.
+- Use live Port Daddy state, source docs, recovery ledgers, WinDAGs skills, and
+  Cartographer ordering before acting.
+- Prefer a truthful halt over fake progress.
+- Leave durable, inspectable evidence for every launch, decision, mutation,
+  review, and handoff.
+- When Port Daddy or WinDAGs is broken, stop routing around it as private
+  friction. Produce a bounded repair, failing repro, or explicit actor handoff.
+- Never let a mutation-capable agent operate as an anonymous process.
+
+This is the conformance contract. The implementation must satisfy this spirit
+even when a specific runtime cannot accept a literal system prompt.
+
+## Runtime Coverage
+
+Provider integration is by adapter, not by copy-pasted prompt strings.
+
+| Runtime | Enforcement surface |
+|---|---|
+| Claude Code | launcher wrapper, plugin/skill install, MCP config, AGENTS/CLAUDE context, output review |
+| Claude CLI / SDK | system/developer message wrapper where available, launch metadata, cost/readiness gate |
+| Codex CLI | `codex exec` wrapper, sandbox/workspace policy, AGENTS context, output-last-message capture |
+| Gemini | Gemini settings / GEMINI.md context plus Port Daddy launcher wrapper |
+| Cloudflare Workers AI | brokered API call wrapper, model ladder, exact telemetry |
+| Moonshot/Kimi | Cloudflare model-ladder entry plus brokered wrapper |
+| Ollama | local broker wrapper, manual readiness until exact telemetry is proven |
+| Aider / custom | environment + stdin wrapper, explicit capability envelope, strict output contract |
+
+Port Daddy can fully enforce only the calls it launches or brokers. For an
+already-open external chat session, Port Daddy can install AGENTS/skills/MCP
+context and later reject unproven changes at PR/guard/CI time, but it cannot
+retroactively become that chat's true system message.
+
+## Conformance And Repair Flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+  A["Operator directive"] --> B["Sensemaker halt gate"]
+  B --> C["Cartographer directive regression"]
+  C --> D["WinDAGs skill search and graft"]
+  D --> E["Node contracts and scope matrix"]
+  E --> F["unSpider risk sweep"]
+  F --> G{"Conformance record valid?"}
+  G -->|no| H["Block launch and file repair/handoff"]
+  G -->|yes| I["Provider wrapper builds final prompt"]
+  I --> J["Launch in harbor/worktree/sandbox"]
+  J --> K["Cheap reviewer checks output"]
+  K --> L{"Pass?"}
+  L -->|no| M["Fix, re-run, or escalate"]
+  L -->|yes| N["Record evidence, PR review, merge gate"]
+```
+
+Tool failure is product feedback:
+
+- If `pd status`, `pd begin`, claims, guard, WinDAGs MCP, or skill grafting
+  fails, the agent must pause feature work.
+- If the failure is bounded and safe, fix it in the same slice.
+- If it is not bounded, create a minimal repro, leave a `pd note` or actor
+  inbox message, and mark the launch blocked.
+- A launch that silently ignores broken Port Daddy/WinDAGs substrate is
+  non-conformant.
+
+## Harbors, Containers, And Network / MCP Access
+
+Harbor remains the product abstraction. Worktree, sandbox, container, VM, or
+remote workspace are implementation strategies behind it.
+
+A harbor policy must describe:
+
+- filesystem read roots and write roots
+- whether copies are full, sparse, overlay, or bind-mounted
+- whether writeback is automatic, patch-based, or human-gated

